          "filename": "Holy relic sites map of Andhra Pradesh.jpg",
          "caption": "Buddhist sites map of Andhra Pradesh.\nThe excavated Buddhist sites which have yielded relic caskets during excavations in the state of Andhra Pradesh (numbered below and match those in the map above)\n\nSalihundam\nRamatheertham\nPavurallakonda\nBavikonda\nShankaram \nKotturu \nTimmapuram \nKodavali \nGuntupalle \nGudivada \nGhantasala \nBhattiprolu \nVaddamanu \nGummadidurru \nAmaravati\nJaggayyapeta \nNagarjunakonda\nOther major Buddhist sites in Andhradesa from the 2nd-century BCE to 5th century CE.\n\nKalingapatnam\nDantapuram\nMukhalingam\nThotlakonda\nAdurru \nAlluru \nAnupu \nChandavaram \nNadaluru \nYerragudi \nNote: The map is created for information and educational purposes. People using the map outside Wikipedia projects are requested to attribute it to the Author below.",
